{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792483083,"nonce":"MDNZR0VbGfBXOp9de++inMy3WeM=","title":"TypeScript: infer native function returns without annotations","message":"The initial zyntax_ts frontend rejects every unannotated function return, including function twice(x: number) { return x * 2; }. Implement return inference for the existing native representations, including forward/dependent calls, scalar and string results, fixed-layout reference objects and no-value functions. Cache inferred signatures and reuse each lowered body instead of reparsing or relowering dependency chains. Preserve readonly views, borrowed/fresh return facts, strict parameter checks and interpreter-first execution.\n\nMatch the pinned TypeScript compiler's acceptance and runtime output. Unresolved recursive inference, heterogeneous unions and possibly undefined returns require their own representation/inference work and must remain explicit tracked gaps rather than guessed scalar types or a permanent restriction. Annotated signatures must still anchor recursive call groups. Extend the differential cases and ownership/tier checks, remove the original inferred-return expected failure, and leave the broader compatibility parent open: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5.","files":null}]}